#: ../../../get_started.md:12
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:14
msgid ""
"Simply pip install `sphinx-design` and add the extension to your `conf.py`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:16
msgid "extensions = [\"sphinx_design\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:20
msgid ""
"For using with [MyST Parser](https://github.com/executablebooks/myst-"
"parser), for Markdown documentation, it is recommended to use the "
"`colon_fence` syntax extension:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:22
msgid ""
"extensions = [\"myst_parser\", \"sphinx_design\"]\n"
"myst_enable_extensions = [\"colon_fence\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:28
msgid ""
"The MyST Markdown examples in this documentation assume that certain "
"optional [MyST syntax extensions](https://myst-parser.readthedocs.io/en/"
"latest/syntax/optional.html) are enabled — extend the "
"`myst_enable_extensions` list shown above with them as needed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:30
msgid ""
"`colon_fence`: used by all examples, to write directives delimited by `:::` "
"fences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:31
msgid ""
"`html_image`: only for examples using raw HTML `<img>` tags, such as the "
"avatar images in [CSS Classes](./css_classes.md)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:32
msgid ""
"`attrs_inline`: only for examples adding attributes to inline elements, such "
"as the links to synchronised [Tabs](./tabs.md)"
msgstr ""

