#: ../../../get_started.md:65
msgid "Creating custom directives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:70
msgid ""
"You can use the `sd_custom_directives` configuration option in your "
"`conf.py` to add custom directives, with default option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:72
msgid ""
"sd_custom_directives = {\n"
"    \"dropdown-syntax\": {\n"
"        \"inherit\": \"dropdown\",\n"
"        \"argument\": \"Syntax\",\n"
"        \"options\": {\n"
"            \"color\": \"primary\",\n"
"            \"icon\": \"code\",\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:85
msgid ""
"The key is the new directive name to add, and the value is a dictionary with "
"the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:87
msgid "`inherit`: The directive to inherit from (e.g. `dropdown`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:88
msgid ""
"`argument`: The default argument (optional, only for directives that take a "
"single argument)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:89
msgid "`options`: A dictionary of default options for the directive (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:92
msgid ""
"For presets beyond default option values, see the [sphinx-ub-directives]"
"(https://sphinx-ub-directives.readthedocs.io) package, from the [sphinx-"
"needs](https://github.com/useblocks/sphinx-needs) project, whose directive "
"presets accept sphinx-design directives (such as `dropdown`) as a base. It "
"adds appended and forced option values, need-type bases (with sphinx-needs), "
"and template directives, and its presets can also be configured in "
"`ubproject.toml`, which [ubCode](https://ubcode.useblocks.com/) reads. To "
"preset a badge's tooltip, see the badge roles' {ref}`tooltip role option <sd-"
"badge-tooltip-option>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:102
msgid "Supported browsers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:104
msgid ""
"sphinx-design targets [**Baseline** Widely Available](https://web.dev/"
"baseline) web features — those interoperable across Chrome, Edge, Firefox "
"and Safari for at least 30 months (in practice, the evergreen browsers of "
"roughly the last 2½ years). Internet Explorer is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:109
msgid ""
"Individual features may additionally use *Baseline Newly Available* CSS "
"where it degrades gracefully; such exceptions are noted in the relevant "
"feature's documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:113
msgid "Migrating from sphinx-panels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:115
msgid ""
"This package arose as an iteration on [sphinx-panels](https://github.com/"
"executablebooks/sphinx-panels), with the intention to make it more flexible, "
"easier to use, and minimise CSS clashes wth sphinx themes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:117
msgid "Notable changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:119
msgid "Reduce direct use of CSS classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:121
msgid "These are replaced by the use of directive options, which are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:123
msgid "Easier to understand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:124
msgid "Easier to validate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:125
msgid "Easier to work with non-HTML outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:126
msgid "Easier to improve/refactor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:128
msgid "`panel` directive replaced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:130
msgid ""
"The `panel` directive is replaced by the use of the top-level `grid` "
"directive, then using `grid-item-card` directive children, rather than "
"delimiting cards by `---`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:133
msgid ""
"If no card is needed, then the `grid-item` directive can be used instead and "
"`card` can be also used independently of grids."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:135
msgid ""
"Approximately, `.. panels::` is equivalent to `.. grid:: 1 2 2 2` with "
"option `:gutter: 2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:137
msgid "`tabbed` directive replaced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:139
msgid ""
"The `tabbed` directive is replaced by the use of the top-level `tab-set` "
"directive, then using `tab-item` directive children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:142
msgid "The `:sync:` option allows to synchronize tab selection across sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:144
msgid ""
"The `tab-set-code` directive provides a shorthand for synced code examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:146
msgid "`link-button` directive replaced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:148
msgid ""
"The `link-button` directive is replaced by the use of `button-ref`/`button-"
"link`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:150
msgid "Directive options have also been added to replace the use of classes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:152
msgid "`stretched-link` -> `:click-parent:`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:153
msgid "`btn-block` -> `:expand:`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:155
msgid "`octicon` icon role"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:157
msgid ""
"The default SVGs produced are now sized relative to the surrounding text "
"(i.e. using `1em`). The syntax for specifying a custom size and adding "
"classes is also changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:160
msgid ""
"This is similar for favicon icons, where the `,` delimiter is also replaced "
"by `;`, e.g. ``:fa:`name,class` `` -> ``:fa:`name;class` ``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:162
msgid "Improved CSS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:164
msgid ""
"Updated Bootstrap CSS from v4 -> v5, which in particular allows top-level "
"grid to define both column numbers and gutter sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:167
msgid ""
"All CSS classes are prefixed with `sd-` (no clash with other theme/extension "
"CSS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started.md:169
msgid "All colors use CSS variables (customisable)"
msgstr ""
